aims-os-desktop-dev (2.1+1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Drop gradle and kotlin. Trixie froze them at 4.4.1 (2017) and
    1.3.31 (2019); no modern Android project builds with either.
    Android Studio (Flatpak) bundles current versions of both, and
    command-line builds go through each project's gradle-wrapper.
  * Depend on adb and fastboot, the real Trixie package names, instead
    of the android-tools-adb / android-tools-fastboot virtual aliases.

 -- AIMS Senegal IT <hakim@aims-senegal.org>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:10:00 +0000

aims-os-desktop-dev (2.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Carved out of aims-os-desktop. Holds the Java /
    Android / Web / Rust / Containers stack (default-jdk, Gradle, Kotlin,
    PHP, Composer, adb/fastboot, Docker, Podman, kubectl, Ansible,
    rustup) — about 2 GB on disk. Kept out of the live ISO; available
    on demand via the first-boot wizard or apt.

 -- AIMS Senegal IT <hakim@aims-senegal.org>  Wed, 27 May 2026 03:00:00 +0000
